      "answer": "dobrze",
      "explain": "Nothing is being described here — there is no noun. When you say how something went, Polish uses the adverb dobrze. Dobra / dobre / dobry only ever attach to a noun."
    },
    {
      "prompt": "Kawa była ___.",
      "choices": [
        "dobra",
        "dobrze",
        "dobre",
        "dobry"
      ],
      "answer": "dobra",
      "explain": "Here there IS a noun — kawa, feminine — so it takes the adjective dobra. Swap the noun out and you are back to było dobrze."
    },
    {
      "prompt": "___ w porządku.",
      "choices": [
        "Wszystko",
        "Nic",
        "Jak",
        "Co"
      ],
      "answer": "Wszystko"
    },
    {
      "prompt": "Someone asks Co słychać? and you have no news. You say:",
      "choices": [
        "Nic nowego.",
        "Jak było?",
        "Było super.",
        "Co słychać?"
      ],
      "answer": "Nic nowego.",
      "explain": "Nic means nothing, and after nic Polish switches to the genitive — hence nowego, not nowy. Keep the two words together."
    },
    {
      "prompt": "— Co słychać? — Nic ___.",
      "choices": [
        "nowego",
        "nowy",
        "nowa",
        "nowe"
      ],
      "answer": "nowego",
      "explain": "Nic nowego is a set answer — 'nothing new'. Nowego is nowy in the genitive, the case Polish reaches for after nic. Take the phrase as one unit."
    },
    {
      "prompt": "It was great. →",
      "choices": [
        "Było super.",
        "Było fajnie.",
        "Wszystko dobrze.",
        "Jak było?"
      ],
      "answer": "Było super.",
      "explain": "Super is borrowed and never changes its ending — no -a, no -e, no -o, whatever you are talking about."
    },
    {
      "prompt": "It was nice. →",
      "choices": [
        "Było fajnie.",
        "Było dobrze.",
        "Nic nowego.",
        "Co słychać?"
      ],
      "answer": "Było fajnie."
    },
    {
      "prompt": "What were you doing yesterday? (to a woman) →",
      "choices": [
        "Co robiłaś wczoraj?",
        "Co robiłeś wczoraj?",
        "Co robiła wczoraj?",
        "Jak było wczoraj?"
      ],
      "answer": "Co robiłaś wczoraj?",
      "explain": "Speaking TO a woman gives -aś, the same ending as byłaś. Robiła with no -ś would mean she was doing, not you."
    },
    {
      "prompt": "— Cześć! Co słychać? — ___",
      "choices": [
        "Wszystko w porządku.",
        "Jak było?",
        "Co robiłeś wczoraj?",
        "Jak było w weekend?"
      ],
      "answer": "Wszystko w porządku.",
      "explain": "Co słychać? is a question, so it needs an answer back — not another question."
    },
